messages.content:
Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: bfd/coffgen.c
Line: 645
Function: bfd_coff_read_internal_relocs
Bug type: integer-overflow
CWE: CWE-190
Explanation: The size for the internal relocation array is computed with amt = sec->reloc_count * sizeof(struct internal_reloc). On 32-bit size_t, this multiplication can overflow for large sec->reloc_count, resulting in allocating a too-small buffer. The subsequent loop (lines 656–657) iterates based on relsz * sec->reloc_count (also subject to modulo wrap), and writes through irel++, which can exceed the allocated buffer, causing a heap buffer overflow.

Source context:
```c
      605: {
      606:   bfd_size_type relsz;
      607:   bfd_byte *free_external = NULL;
      608:   struct internal_reloc *free_internal = NULL;
      609:   bfd_byte *erel;
      610:   bfd_byte *erel_end;
      611:   struct internal_reloc *irel;
      612:   bfd_size_type amt;
      613: 
      614:   if (sec->reloc_count == 0)
      615:     return internal_relocs;	/* Nothing to do.  */
      616: 
      617:   if (coff_section_data (abfd, sec) != NULL
      618:       && coff_section_data (abfd, sec)->relocs != NULL)
      619:     {
      620:       if (! require_internal)
      621: 	return coff_section_data (abfd, sec)->relocs;
      622:       memcpy (internal_relocs, coff_section_data (abfd, sec)->relocs,
      623: 	      sec->reloc_count * sizeof (struct internal_reloc));
      624:       return internal_relocs;
      625:     }
